		</wp:postmeta>
		<wp:postmeta>
			<wp:meta_key><![CDATA[_lb_document_data]]></wp:meta_key>
			<wp:meta_value><![CDATA[{"version":"2.8","root":[{"id":"canvasly-overview-logo","type":"image","settings":{"image_url":"https://canvasly.pro/assets/canvasly-logo.png","alt":"Canvasly. Design your pages visually.","link_to":"custom","link":"https://canvasly.pro","link_target":"_self","alignment":"left","width":"120px","height":"96px","object_fit":"contain"},"styles":{"base":{}},"children":[]},{"id":"canvasly-overview-wrap","type":"container","settings":{},"styles":{"base":{}},"children":[{"id":"canvasly-overview-body","type":"html","settings":{"html":"    <nav class=\"crumbs\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n      <ol>\n        <li aria-current=\"page\">Canvasly</li>\n      </ol>\n    </nav>\n    <header class=\"page-intro\">\n      <h1>Canvasly documentation</h1>\n      <p class=\"lede\">Canvasly is a visual page builder for WordPress. Design a page on a canvas, then publish it in WordPress. Covers install, settings, units, shortcodes, AI and MCP.</p>\n      <p class=\"meta\">Updated <time datetime=\"2026-09-23\">September 23, 2026</time>. Covers Canvasly 0.12.76 and Canvasly Pro 0.6.3.</p>\n    </header>\n\n    <figure>\n      <img src=\"assets/editor-layout.svg\" alt=\"Sketch of the Canvasly editor: a dark top bar with Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile, a left Units library, a center page canvas, and a right Settings panel with Content, Style, and Advanced tabs.\" width=\"880\" height=\"420\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n      <figcaption>The editor has a unit library on the left, the page in the middle, and the selected unit’s settings on the right.</figcaption>\n    </figure>\n\n    <article>\n      <h2>What you can do</h2>\n      <ul>\n        <li>Open a page or post and choose <strong>Edit with Canvasly</strong>, or use the same link in the WordPress admin bar.</li>\n        <li>Drag units such as Heading, Image, Button, Container, and Grid onto the page.</li>\n        <li>Switch the canvas between desktop, tablet, and mobile. Extra sizes can be turned on under Design System.</li>\n        <li>Save reusable templates, then place them with a shortcode, a WordPress block, a Canvasly Template unit, or a sidebar widget.</li>\n        <li>With Canvasly Pro, design a header and footer, popups, shop layouts (when WooCommerce is installed), and payment buttons.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>These pages describe Canvasly 0.12.76 and Canvasly Pro 0.6.3, as named in the plugin files. WordPress 6.9 or newer and PHP 7.4 or newer are required. The readme lists testing through WordPress 7.1.</p>\n    </article>\n\n    <nav class=\"card toc\" aria-label=\"Table of contents\">\n      <h2>In this guide</h2>\n      <a href=\"/canvasly-price/\">Canvasly Lite vs Canvasly Pro and annual plans</a>\n      <a href=\"/canvasly-install/\">Install and activate Canvasly and Canvasly Pro</a>\n      <a href=\"/canvasly-settings/\">Every setting screen, what each option does, and the default</a>\n      <a href=\"/canvasly-shortcodes/\">Shortcodes you can paste into content</a>\n      <a href=\"/canvasly-units/\">Canvasly units, the Grid, the right-click menu, and the WordPress template block</a>\n      <a href=\"/canvasly-ai/\">Connect an AI agent with AI Connection and MCP</a>\n      <a href=\"/canvasly-faq/\">Common questions, including items still marked for follow-up</a>\n    </nav>\n\n    <section class=\"panel\">\n      <h2>Words used in Canvasly</h2>\n      <dl>\n        <dt>Unit</dt>\n        <dd>A piece you place on the canvas: a heading, a button, a container, a grid, and so on. The left panel is the unit library.</dd>\n        <dt>Container</dt>\n        <dd>A box that holds other units. It cannot be turned off in Units Manager.</dd>\n        <dt>Template</dt>\n        <dd>A saved Canvasly layout. Saved templates live under the Canvasly menu and can be embedded on other pages.</dd>\n        <dt>Design System</dt>\n        <dd>Site-wide colors, fonts, content width, and the widths used for phone, tablet, and larger screens.</dd>\n      </dl>\n    </section>"},"styles":{"base":{}},"children":[]}]}],"header":[],"footer":[],"settings":{"template":"default"}}]]></wp:meta_value>
		</wp:postmeta>
