	</item>
	<item>
		<title>Build pages visually with Canvasly</title>
		<link>https://canvasly.pro/canvasly-price/</link>
		<pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:10:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[canvasly]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://canvasly.pro/?page_id=91009</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:html -->
<p class="brand"><a href="https://canvasly.pro"><img class="brand-logo" src="https://canvasly.pro/assets/canvasly-logo.png" alt="Canvasly. Design your pages visually." width="400" height="320" style="height:96px;width:auto;border-radius:12px"></a></p>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/canvasly-overview/">Canvasly</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">Price</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level": 1} -->
<h1 class="wp-block-heading">Build pages visually with Canvasly</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "lede"} -->
<p class="lede">Canvasly is a visual page builder for WordPress. You design a page on a canvas, then publish it the usual WordPress way. Canvasly Pro adds theme parts, shop units, popups, forms logging, payments, and more, and it only runs when Canvasly is active.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "meta"} -->
<p class="meta">Updated <time datetime="2026-09-23">September 23, 2026</time>. Covers Canvasly 0.12.76 and Canvasly Pro 0.6.3.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level": 2, "anchor": "lite-vs-pro"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="lite-vs-pro">Canvasly Lite vs Canvasly Pro</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Canvasly Lite is the free page builder. Canvasly Pro is a second plugin that adds theme, shop, payments, and the rest of the Pro modules. Every Pro plan unlocks the same features. The plans differ by site count. Pro loads only when Lite is active and at least version 0.12.73.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:html -->
<table class="compare-table">
          <caption>Canvasly Lite versus Canvasly Pro</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr class="compare-banner">
              <th scope="col"><strong>Canvasly</strong><span>Feature Comparison</span><em>Two plugins. One document model.</em></th>
              <th scope="col"><strong>Canvasly Lite</strong><span>Free</span><em>Visual page builder</em></th>
              <th scope="col"><strong>Canvasly Pro</strong><span>From $59 / year</span><em>Theme, shop, and payments</em></th>
            </tr>
            <tr class="compare-cols">
              <th scope="col">Feature</th>
              <th scope="col">Lite</th>
              <th scope="col">Pro</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="compare-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Builder</th></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Visual editor</strong><span>Drag-and-drop canvas, nested containers, CSS Grid, desktop, tablet, and mobile.</span></th><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Core elements</strong><span>Heading, text, image, button, gallery, video, tabs, form, price table, collection loop, and the rest of the Lite library.</span></th><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Design system</strong><span>Global colors, typography, variables, classes, components, and site-kit import and export.</span></th><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="mark-text">Kit also carries Pro theme templates</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Style and custom CSS</strong><span>Typography, spacing, borders, shadows, visibility, ARIA, and CSS on the element or the page.</span></th><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Entrance and exit motion</strong><span>CSS presets, custom keyframes, and viewport, load, hover, click, and scroll triggers.</span></th><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Sticky, scroll, and page transitions</strong><span>Stick to top or bottom, scroll opacity, slide, and scale, scroll snap, and page transitions.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr class="compare-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Content</th></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Saved templates</strong><span>Shortcode, Gutenberg block, template widget, or sidebar widget.</span></th><td><span class="mark-text">Page templates</span></td><td><span class="mark-text">Also header, footer, popup, loop item, section</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Collection loop</strong><span>Query posts or terms, with numbered, previous-next, or load-more pagination.</span></th><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span class="mark-text">Loop-item templates and a taxonomy filter</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Dynamic tags</strong><span>Values that resolve in the editor and on the front end.</span></th><td><span class="mark-text">Post, author, site, user, archive, term</span></td><td><span class="mark-text">Plus request, custom fields, ACF, product price and SKU</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Forms</strong><span>Lite keeps the form element. Pro extends fields and what happens after submit.</span></th><td><span class="mark-text">One email</span></td><td><span class="mark-text">Email, redirect, webhook, submissions log, CSV</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Extra form fields</strong><span>Number, date, radio, acceptance, and file upload.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Pro elements</strong><span>Call to action, countdown, carousels, hotspot, price list, off-canvas, Lottie, video playlist, and the rest of the Pro set.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr class="compare-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Theme</th></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Theme Builder</strong><span>Header, footer, single, archive, search, 404, and section, with display rules.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Theme elements</strong><span>Site identity, the current post, archives, author, comments, breadcrumbs, search, and a sitemap.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Popups</strong><span>Load, scroll, click, exit, and inactivity triggers. A link can open one.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Display conditions</strong><span>Hide one element by role, login, date, author, taxonomy, or URL parameter.</span></th><td><span class="mark-text">Device visibility only</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Menus</strong><span>WordPress menus with dropdowns, and a mega menu from a section template.</span></th><td><span class="mark-text">Site navigation element</span></td><td><span class="mark-text">Nav Menu and mega menu</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Custom code, fonts, and icons</strong><span>Site-wide snippets, uploaded font files, and extra icon sets.</span></th><td><span class="mark-text">Per-element CSS, Google Fonts, icon manager</span></td><td><span class="mark-text">Site snippets, uploaded fonts, custom icon sets</span></td></tr>
            <tr class="compare-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Shop</th></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>WooCommerce templates</strong><span>Product and product-archive locations. Unloaded without WooCommerce.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark-text">When WooCommerce is active</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Product and cart elements</strong><span>Product parts, menu cart, and notices. Cart, checkout, and my account print WooCommerce forms.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark-text">When WooCommerce is active</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Hosted payments</strong><span>Stripe, PayPal, Square, Razorpay, Mollie, and Authorize.net. Card data stays on the gateway.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr class="compare-group"><th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Platform</th></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Editor notes</strong><span>Notes on a node for people who can edit. Not public comments.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>AI connection</strong><span>AI connection, MCP host, and the layout-schema API.</span></th><td><span class="mark no" aria-label="Not included">✗</span></td><td><span class="mark yes" aria-label="Included">✓</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row"><strong>License</strong><span>An inactive key blocks new Pro elements and Pro REST routes.</span></th><td><span class="mark-text">No license</span></td><td><span class="mark-text">Annual key, same features on every plan</span></td></tr>
          </tbody>
          <tfoot>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Price</th>
              <td><strong>Free</strong><span>Start building</span></td>
              <td><strong>From $59 / year</strong><span>Same features on every plan</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tfoot>
        </table>
<!-- /wp:html -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "compare-note"} -->
<p class="compare-note">Pro loads only when Lite is active and at least version 0.12.73. WooCommerce elements stay unloaded without WooCommerce. Without a valid Pro key, new Pro elements are dropped on save.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level": 2, "anchor": "plans"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="plans">Licensing</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Choose a Canvasly Pro annual plan. Checkout and license-key delivery are handled on the Canvasly license site.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level": 3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Pro Personal</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "price"} -->
<p class="price">$59 <span>/ year</span></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "pricing-meta"} -->
<p class="pricing-meta">1 site included</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a class="pricing-buy" href="https://license.canvasly.pro/?plan=pro_personal">Purchase Pro Personal</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level": 3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Pro Business</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "price"} -->
<p class="price">$79 <span>/ year</span></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "pricing-meta"} -->
<p class="pricing-meta">5 sites included</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a class="pricing-buy" href="https://license.canvasly.pro/?plan=pro_business">Purchase Pro Business</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level": 3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Pro Agency</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "price"} -->
<p class="price">$129 <span>/ year</span></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "pricing-meta"} -->
<p class="pricing-meta">25 sites included</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a class="pricing-buy" href="https://license.canvasly.pro/?plan=pro_agency">Purchase Pro Agency</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level": 3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Pro Unlimited</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "price"} -->
<p class="price">$199 <span>/ year</span></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"className": "pricing-meta"} -->
<p class="pricing-meta">100 sites included</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a class="pricing-buy" href="https://license.canvasly.pro/?plan=pro_unlimited">Purchase Pro Unlimited</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[Compare Canvasly Lite and Canvasly Pro. Lite is free. Pro annual plans start at $59 and add theme parts, shop units, popups, forms, and payments.]]></excerpt:encoded>
